<section class="log-section">
    <h2>Event lifecycle and what each event proves</h2>
    <p>Every paid PrTask transaction emits the following events in this order. Maya Business reviewers and auditors can request the corresponding rows from the audit log table for any task ID.</p>
    <table class="log-table">
        <tr><th>Event</th><th>What it proves</th><th>Linked artifact</th></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>task.posted</strong></td><td>The cardholder created the task and committed to the no-charge-until-merge model.</td><td>TaskEntity row + Stage 1 email</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>pr.submitted</strong></td><td>A developer responded with a deliverable. No charge yet.</td><td>PullRequestEntity row + Stage 2 email + GitHub PR</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>pr.approval_requested</strong></td><td>The cardholder, authenticated and acting on their own session, initiated the approve action.</td><td>AuditLogEntity row with IP and user agent</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>pr.merged</strong></td><td><strong>Delivery acknowledgment.</strong> The cardholder explicitly accepted the deliverable. The merge commit SHA is content-addressed.</td><td>GitHub merge commit + Stage 3 email + receipt page</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>payment.captured</strong></td><td>Card charged via Maya Business after the cardholder accepted delivery.</td><td>PaymentEntity row with mayaPaymentId</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>email.sent</strong></td><td>SendGrid messageId proves the confirmation email was delivered to the cardholder's verified inbox.</td><td>SendGrid event webhook log</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>receipt.generated</strong></td><td>The deep-linked receipt URL is published and remains available for future reference.</td><td><a href="/Receipt?pr=https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/1">View receipt</a></td></tr>
    </table>
</section>
<section class="log-section">
    <h2>Retention and access</h2>
    <p>System logs are persisted to the <code>AuditLogEntity</code> table in the platform database, replicated daily to a separate snapshot store, and retained for a minimum of five (5) years from the date of the transaction in line with Philippine BSP, BIR, and AMLA recordkeeping requirements. PrTask will produce the corresponding rows on request from the cardholder, Maya Business, or any competent regulator. Contact <a href="mailto:support@prtask.com">support@prtask.com</a> with the receipt number to retrieve a full chronology.</p>
</section>
